From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:29:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: dump_render debug parameters for submitted
 render Works

Log the 3D register table (as the hang report prints it), the 3D
descriptor words at +0x440..+0x700 and +0xb80..+0xc00 and the TA tail
at +0x800..+0x8c0 for every render whose queue ordinal is within
[dump_render_from, dump_render_to], capped by dump_render_max. Each
dump names the client, context, command stream and ordinal, so a stuck
Work from a hang report can be diffed against completed instances.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render parameters log submitted render Works
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_buffered keeps submitted renders for the hang report
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_buffered prints a closing process's renders
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render shape and context filters
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 render ring entries follow their VM, not the closing task
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_recent keeps each context's latest renders

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_buffered keeps submitted renders for the hang report]
Printing every dumped render on the submission path may perturb the
timing of the A4 stall. With dump_render_buffered=N the last N
submitted renders (within dump_render_from/to if set) are copied into a
ring allocated once on first use, and printed oldest first, tagged
"ring", only by the hang report. Each entry keeps the TA and 3D Work
bytes and is printed in the dump_render format.

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_buffered prints a closing process's renders]
Runs that never stall still need the same-run baseline. When a VM is
detached, print the closing process's buffered renders (tagged "exit")
and drop them from the hang report's set.

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render shape and context filters]
dump_render_reg/dump_render_value keep only renders whose 3D register
table holds that register with that value (e.g. 0x15211 for the
framebuffer size), and dump_render_context only those on one firmware
context slot, so the buffered ring holds completed instances of the
stalling pass from the stalling run itself.

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 render ring entries follow their VM, not the closing task]
The DRM file can be torn down from a task other than the client that
submitted, so matching the closing task's tgid could print nothing.
Record the submitting VM's render root and flush by it at detach, and
always log a summary line at detach and in the hang report, so an empty
ring is distinguishable from a hook that never ran.

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 dump_render_recent keeps each context's latest renders]
The shape ring holds other clients' renders of the stuck shape, but
per-context state that changes at the first switch to a new shape only
shows against the same context's own previous renders. Keep a second,
unfiltered ring of the last N renders (dump_render_recent) and print,
in the hang report, those on each stuck render's context, oldest first.
Both rings share one implementation, allocated once on first use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs    |  32 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16.rs         |   6 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs     |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs | 264 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 303 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
index de273f64b281..c4c9f50823e4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
@@ -124,6 +124,38 @@ fn probe<'bound>(
             default: 0,
             description: "Debug: 1 logs each queue's kernel-resolved dependency counts when it is destroyed (TA holds, cross-queue holds, lane-ordered fragment waits, compute holds)",
         },
+        dump_render_from: u32 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: with dump_render_to, log the register table and descriptor words of every render Work whose queue ordinal is in [from, to], at submission, for diffing against hang reports",
+        },
+        dump_render_to: u32 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: last queue ordinal dumped (0 disables dump_render)",
+        },
+        dump_render_reg: u32 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: dump_render only keeps renders whose 3D register table holds this register with value dump_render_value (0: no filter), e.g. 0x15211 = 0x2d000000500 for 1280x720",
+        },
+        dump_render_value: u64 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: the value dump_render_reg must hold",
+        },
+        dump_render_context: u32 {
+            default: 0xffffffff,
+            description: "Debug: dump_render only keeps renders on this firmware context slot (default: any)",
+        },
+        dump_render_recent: u32 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: N > 0 keeps the last N submitted renders of any shape in a second ring; the hang report prints those on each stuck render's context, for diffing against its immediate predecessors",
+        },
+        dump_render_buffered: u32 {
+            default: 0,
+            description: "Debug: N > 0 keeps the last N submitted renders (within dump_render_from/to if set, otherwise all) in a ring and prints them only in the hang report, with no printing on the submission path",
+        },
+        dump_render_max: u32 {
+            default: 400,
+            description: "Debug: at most this many renders are dumped per boot",
+        },
         lifecycle: u32 {
             default: 0,
             description: "Experiment: render lifecycle words (regs 0x1ca10/0x14a1/0xa349 tiling, 0x160e0/0x1499/0xa341 fragment) and Work uuids. 1: unique per render, as Metal: two device-wide counters, the high word +1 and the low word +2 per render (fragment even, tiling odd). 0: the original constants for every render (production)",
